---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /aegis-pdns/test/
title: Test AEGIS PDNS
description: Run browser-side checks for AEGIS PDNS endpoint reachability, DoH behavior, canary behavior, and best-effort device configuration.
---

<section class="stack-xl">
  <div class="fade-up">
    {% set eyebrow = "AEGIS PDNS" %}{% set heading = "Test AEGIS PDNS behavior" %}{% set asH1 = true %}{% set kicker = "checks: reachability · doh query · filter behavior · public canaries · device probe" %}{% set desc = "Run practical browser-side checks against the selected AEGIS PDNS DoH endpoint. The checks separate endpoint health, DNS response parsing, filter behavior, public canary reachability, and best-effort device configuration." %}
    {% include "section-heading.njk" %}
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="verify">
    <h3 class="section-title">Resolver endpoint tests</h3>
    <p>The resolver tests check whether a selected AEGIS endpoint works from this browser. They do not prove that your device is configured to use AEGIS PDNS as its current resolver.</p>

    <div class="field" style="margin-top: 12px;">
      <label for="resolverSelect">Endpoint under test</label>
      <select id="resolverSelect" name="resolver">
        <option value="{{ site.endpoints.doh }}" data-mode="filtered">Filtered: {{ site.endpoints.doh }}</option>
        <option value="{{ site.endpoints.dohOpen }}" data-mode="open">Open: {{ site.endpoints.dohOpen }}</option>
      </select>
      <span class="hint">Mode: <span id="resolverMode">filtered</span></span>
    </div>

    <input type="hidden" id="verifyDohUrl" />
    <div class="note" style="margin-top: 12px;">
      <div class="mono">Allow canary: <span id="allowHost">{{ site.endpoints.allowTestHost }}</span></div>
      <div class="mono">Block canary: <span id="blockHost">{{ site.endpoints.blockTestHost }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="statusline">
      <span class="pill"><span class="led" id="vLed"></span><span id="vStatus">Idle</span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="btnrow">
      <button class="btn primary" type="button" onclick="verifyAll()">Run all checks</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyReachability()">Endpoint reachability</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyBinaryExample()">DoH query</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyBlockTest()">Filter behavior</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="verifyPublicCanaries()">Public canaries</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="clearVerify()">Reset</button>
    </div>

    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>1. Endpoint reachability</h3>
        <p><strong id="rReach">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dReach"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>2. DoH query correctness</h3>
        <p><strong id="rBin">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dBin"></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dBinExtra"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>3. Filter behavior</h3>
        <p><strong id="rBlock">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dBlock"></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dBlockExtra"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>4. Public canary reachability</h3>
        <p><strong id="rPublic">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dPublic"></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dPublicExtra"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>5. Device configuration</h3>
        <p><strong id="rDevice">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dDevice"></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dDeviceExtra"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Result summary</h3>
        <p><strong id="rSummary">Idle</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="vSummary"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="device-probe">
    <h3 class="section-title">Is this device using AEGIS PDNS?</h3>
    <p>The device probe checks whether this browser or device appears to be configured to use AEGIS PDNS as its current resolver. It is best-effort because browsers do not expose the active system resolver directly.</p>
    <p class="mini">The resolver tests above check whether a selected AEGIS endpoint works from this browser. The device probe checks whether this browser or device is actually configured to use AEGIS PDNS as its current resolver.</p>

    <div class="note">
      <div class="mono">Control: <span id="controlHost">{{ site.endpoints.controlHost }}</span></div>
      <div class="mono">Allow: <span id="deviceAllowHost">{{ site.endpoints.allowTestHost }}</span></div>
      <div class="mono">Block: <span id="deviceBlockHost">{{ site.endpoints.blockTestHost }}</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="statusline">
      <span class="pill"><span class="led" id="overallLed"></span><span id="overallText">Idle</span></span>
      <button class="btn primary" type="button" onclick="runAll()">Run device probe</button>
    </div>

    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3><span class="led" id="dohLed" style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 6px;"></span>Control host</h3>
        <p><strong id="dohText">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="dohDetail"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3><span class="led" id="blockLed" style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 6px;"></span>Block canary</h3>
        <p><strong id="blockText">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="blockDetail"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3><span class="led" id="deviceLed" style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 6px;"></span>This device</h3>
        <p><strong id="deviceText">Not run</strong></p>
        <p class="mini" id="deviceDetail"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>DoT and DoQ validation</h3>
    <p>Standard browser JavaScript cannot normally open raw TCP/853 for DoT or UDP/QUIC/853 for DoQ. This page labels DoT and DoQ as configuration endpoints, not browser-tested protocols.</p>
    <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 10px;"><span class="lang">shell</span><span class="cmt"># Manual DoT connectivity check</span>
openssl s_client -connect {{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}:{{ site.endpoints.dotPort }} -servername {{ site.endpoints.dotHost }}</div>
  </div>

  <p class="mini">
    <a href="/aegis-pdns/">Back to AEGIS PDNS</a>
    <span style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.20);"> · </span>
    <a href="{{ site.github.aegisDnsIssues }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report DNS issue</a>
  </p>
</section>
